(5014302, 731110, 96721, '<td valign="top">Nice dog portrait but the angle could have been more fitting to upside down, this one makes him look more like he is on his side unfortunately.<br/> <br/>Very nice mood in the eyes though<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Nice dog portrait but the angle could have been more fitting to upside down, this one makes him look more like he is on his side unfortunately. Very nice mood in the eyes though Comment Only', '2008-10-19 09:53:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014306, 730755, 96721, '<td valign="top">The lighting looks a bit harsh at the top of the can and to be honest it''s a little uninspiring, it does however fit the challenge! which seems to be a bit of a feat for this one ;)<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'The lighting looks a bit harsh at the top of the can and to be honest it''s a little uninspiring, it does however fit the challenge! which seems to be a bit of a feat for this one ;) Comment Only', '2008-10-19 09:55:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014311, 731157, 96721, '<td valign="top">This is a very interesting image, I like it a lot, the greens and whites work so wonderfully together. Not sure if it is my eyes or not but it looks like it could do with straightening ever so slightly.<br/> <br/>I think I would have given this an 8 had I been voting.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'This is a very interesting image, I like it a lot, the greens and whites work so wonderfully together. Not sure if it is my eyes or not but it looks like it could do with straightening ever so slightly. I think I would have given this an 8 had I been voting. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 09:56:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014313, 731156, 96721, '<td valign="top">Rotated image<br/> <br/>Personally I would have marked all rotated / flipped images without a reflection as DNMC and scored them between 2 and 4<br/> <br/>This one is not very sharp, looks a bit too heavily saturated so probably would have been a 2 sorry :(<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Rotated image Personally I would have marked all rotated / flipped images without a reflection as DNMC and scored them between 2 and 4 This one is not very sharp, looks a bit too heavily saturated so probably would have been a 2 sorry :( Comment Only', '2008-10-19 09:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014314, 730992, 96721, '<td valign="top">Quite a funny take on the challenge, and very nicely cropped and presented.<br/> <br/>Not sure what I would have given this had I been voting, it meets the challenge with the duck being upside down so most likely a 6 it is quite nicely shot, although I can''t quite make out if there is a yellow cast to this?<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Quite a funny take on the challenge, and very nicely cropped and presented. Not sure what I would have given this had I been voting, it meets the challenge with the duck being upside down so most likely a 6 it is quite nicely shot, although I can''t quite make out if there is a yellow cast to this? Comment Only', '2008-10-19 09:59:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014315, 730902, 96721, '<td valign="top">Love the line of the birds flying across this, not sure which is the reflection and which is the true subject, not that it matters for this shot as theres enough of the reflection either way. <br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Love the line of the birds flying across this, not sure which is the reflection and which is the true subject, not that it matters for this shot as theres enough of the reflection either way.  Comment Only', '2008-10-19 10:01:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014317, 730727, 96721, '<td valign="top">Good capture, not sure if there is enough tone in this due to trying to bring the sky back? maybe it was just a really flat boring sky though but the whites don''t really pop so I am wondering.<br/> <br/>Obviously a pretty unique shot though and for that I think it will do quite well.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Good capture, not sure if there is enough tone in this due to trying to bring the sky back? maybe it was just a really flat boring sky though but the whites don''t really pop so I am wondering. Obviously a pretty unique shot though and for that I think it will do quite well. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 10:02:45.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5014318, 731021, 96721, '<td valign="top">Good B&amp;W conversion with a nice tonal range throughout the shot.<br/> <br/>The only thing lacking is Wow factor. The right hand glass looks a little water stained at the bottom too which is a little distracting.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Good B&W conversion with a nice tonal range throughout the shot. The only thing lacking is Wow factor. The right hand glass looks a little water stained at the bottom too which is a little distracting. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 10:04:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014320, 731023, 96721, '<td valign="top">Hmm quite a clever shot, immediate thought was ANOTHER ROTATED IMAGED!!! <br/> <br/>But after looking for a little while I noticed that the model is actually upside in that tube which means it is not a DNMC ;)<br/> <br/>would have been a 7 or 8 I think had I been voting.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Hmm quite a clever shot, immediate thought was ANOTHER ROTATED IMAGED!!!  But after looking for a little while I noticed that the model is actually upside in that tube which means it is not a DNMC ;) would have been a 7 or 8 I think had I been voting. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 10:05:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014321, 730201, 96721, '<td valign="top">Sorry I don''t like the lighting, the composition or the subject, it just looks like a rotated image as well which I would have marked them all DNMC without a true upside down take on the challenge (ie at least a reflection).<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Sorry I don''t like the lighting, the composition or the subject, it just looks like a rotated image as well which I would have marked them all DNMC without a true upside down take on the challenge (ie at least a reflection). Comment Only', '2008-10-19 10:06:33.000000', NULL, 1),
