(5014521, 730357, 96721, '<td valign="top">The image is upside down I get that, but that is all I can see in the shot that is, I would really have liked this shot a lot more had you attempted to make it look like the model was upside down in the room, ie the lamp positioned above the picture pointing downwards as if on a table (where I suspect it is now but pointing the wrong way), I think had you taken this idea further you could have had a really great shot.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'The image is upside down I get that, but that is all I can see in the shot that is, I would really have liked this shot a lot more had you attempted to make it look like the model was upside down in the room, ie the lamp positioned above the picture pointing downwards as if on a table (where I suspect it is now but pointing the wrong way), I think had you taken this idea further you could have had a really great shot. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:06:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014522, 730362, 96721, '<td valign="top">I had a similar shot to this with a clear plastic mat under the glass.<br/> <br/>The biggest problem I see with your shot is that the lighting is very flat and this make the whole image look a bit drab and would be all but impossible to get the glass and fluid to "pop" looks pretty well focused though and there also looks to be a really nice reflection on that glass, had the lighting been better I think this could have scored really well.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'I had a similar shot to this with a clear plastic mat under the glass. The biggest problem I see with your shot is that the lighting is very flat and this make the whole image look a bit drab and would be all but impossible to get the glass and fluid to "pop" looks pretty well focused though and there also looks to be a really nice reflection on that glass, had the lighting been better I think this could have scored really well. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:08:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014525, 730909, 96721, '<td valign="top">Nice idea<br/> <br/>Pretty well lit especially the vase and rose although it''s a bit of a shame about the window reflection right over the rose anywhere else and it wouldn''t have caused quite as much distraction. The ring could do with a bit more light to help emphasise it as it is a bit lost in the whole picture.<br/> <br/>Good shot though and I would be surprised if this doesn''t make the top 20<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Nice idea Pretty well lit especially the vase and rose although it''s a bit of a shame about the window reflection right over the rose anywhere else and it wouldn''t have caused quite as much distraction. The ring could do with a bit more light to help emphasise it as it is a bit lost in the whole picture. Good shot though and I would be surprised if this doesn''t make the top 20 Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:11:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014530, 731063, 96721, '<td valign="top">I am assuming you have done a double exposure which is quite effective, I like the way the lighting effectively falls on the same side of the face and at first I actually thought this was a copy / paste / rotate but the lighting is just different enough to prove that wrong :)<br/> <br/>Not sure how this will score, it must have been pretty hard to pull off this well and it is artistic, but I wonder if some people will think it a DQ for the reasons I mention above...<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'I am assuming you have done a double exposure which is quite effective, I like the way the lighting effectively falls on the same side of the face and at first I actually thought this was a copy / paste / rotate but the lighting is just different enough to prove that wrong :) Not sure how this will score, it must have been pretty hard to pull off this well and it is artistic, but I wonder if some people will think it a DQ for the reasons I mention above... Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:13:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014532, 730315, 96721, '<td valign="top">Looks to have a heavy yellow cast to the whole image, the lighting is very flat and whatever it is you are holding in your left hand is very distracting.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Looks to have a heavy yellow cast to the whole image, the lighting is very flat and whatever it is you are holding in your left hand is very distracting. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014535, 731152, 96721, '<td valign="top">Quite a clever shot, I am not sure if that is a ray of light shooting in to the glass with smoke bellowing out or whether it is someone blowing a very fine smoke trail in to the glass, my main gripe with the shot is the lighting is so harsh at the base of the glass bowl and that really detracts from an otherwise fine shot.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Quite a clever shot, I am not sure if that is a ray of light shooting in to the glass with smoke bellowing out or whether it is someone blowing a very fine smoke trail in to the glass, my main gripe with the shot is the lighting is so harsh at the base of the glass bowl and that really detracts from an otherwise fine shot. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:16:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014538, 730791, 96721, '<td valign="top">Heh original take on the challenge that I think many will be able to associate with. My main points of CC would be that there is maybe slightly too much blur on the hand, and the image is overall quite dark. Actually it could probably do with a slightly stronger composition with more cropped from the right.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Heh original take on the challenge that I think many will be able to associate with. My main points of CC would be that there is maybe slightly too much blur on the hand, and the image is overall quite dark. Actually it could probably do with a slightly stronger composition with more cropped from the right. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014543, 730552, 96721, '<td valign="top">There are a lot of these shots in the challenge and some really hit the mark and others whilst very nice don''t really come with the WOW factor.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately yours is in the latter category for me and I think this is due to the very straight lines across the image, the two signs on the left are a bit distracting and that forground item is a bit distracting IMHO.<br/> <br/>They are some wonderful autumnal colours though and must have been a sight to behold<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'There are a lot of these shots in the challenge and some really hit the mark and others whilst very nice don''t really come with the WOW factor. Unfortunately yours is in the latter category for me and I think this is due to the very straight lines across the image, the two signs on the left are a bit distracting and that forground item is a bit distracting IMHO. They are some wonderful autumnal colours though and must have been a sight to behold Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:23:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014551, 731129, 96721, '<td valign="top">Good idea with the splash but I think the bottom is cropped far too hard, and whilst I think I get the idea to make it look like a natural scene up the right way with the splash being almost abstract and like it is falling out of the sky I think the whole image is made to look very dark and unbalanced because of it.<br/> <br/>ETA: Ahh I see the title gives it more meaning, hmm I normally look at the title too must have missed this... I still think the comments above are valid though.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'Good idea with the splash but I think the bottom is cropped far too hard, and whilst I think I get the idea to make it look like a natural scene up the right way with the splash being almost abstract and like it is falling out of the sky I think the whole image is made to look very dark and unbalanced because of it. ETA: Ahh I see the title gives it more meaning, hmm I normally look at the title too must have missed this... I still think the comments above are valid though. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:26:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5014555, 730933, 96721, '<td valign="top">I love the tone of this image, I think the bridge is just a bit too fussy though and I might have been tempted to look for either a higher view point to allow a similar shot with less of the bridge in it, or I might just have cropped tighter at the bottom (not sure how that would have balanced the image though).<br/> <br/>Actually as I look at the image I think that grey building on the left could be cropped out almost making for a square crop and that would lessen the impact of the bridge I think.<br/> <br/>Comment Only</td>', 'I love the tone of this image, I think the bridge is just a bit too fussy though and I might have been tempted to look for either a higher view point to allow a similar shot with less of the bridge in it, or I might just have cropped tighter at the bottom (not sure how that would have balanced the image though). Actually as I look at the image I think that grey building on the left could be cropped out almost making for a square crop and that would lessen the impact of the bridge I think. Comment Only', '2008-10-19 13:29:14.000000', NULL, 1),
