(5019775, 731023, 89341, '<td valign="top">I really like this, it''s a clever idea. The colours are good and bright.<br/> <br/>cc. I would like the person to be a bit larger in the frame, you are really limited by the 640px though so that''s tough, you may loose the effect by cropping in a bit.<br/> <br/>Maybe you were hurt with some DNMC votes if people thought the image was just rotated without studying it more</td>', 'I really like this, it''s a clever idea. The colours are good and bright. cc. I would like the person to be a bit larger in the frame, you are really limited by the 640px though so that''s tough, you may loose the effect by cropping in a bit. Maybe you were hurt with some DNMC votes if people thought the image was just rotated without studying it more', '2008-10-22 04:04:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(5019813, 730318, 75720, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your votes and helpful comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-11-01 21:17:42.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for your votes and helpful comments.', '2008-10-22 04:15:01.000000', '2008-11-01 21:17:42.000000', 0),
(5019848, 730293, 28742, '<td valign="top">I think it''s a great shot. As far as the challenge goes, I didn''t vote, but I would lean toward a DNMC score (5-ish) because technically spiders really can''t be upside down - unless they were on their back, IMO. Not a blatant DNMC, but I''d put it there with people who rotated their camera or photo 180°. Call me a nitpicking, narrow minded troll. :)</td>', 'I think it''s a great shot. As far as the challenge goes, I didn''t vote, but I would lean toward a DNMC score (5-ish) because technically spiders really can''t be upside down - unless they were on their back, IMO. Not a blatant DNMC, but I''d put it there with people who rotated their camera or photo 180°. Call me a nitpicking, narrow minded troll. :)', '2008-10-22 05:07:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(5019849, 730293, 99263, '<td valign="top">This was one of my faves from the start from a technical point of view and that 9 on the chart was given by me.</td>', 'This was one of my faves from the start from a technical point of view and that 9 on the chart was given by me.', '2008-10-22 05:10:09.000000', NULL, 0),
